    "problem_statement": "## Background\nA warehouse manager tracks daily stock additions across `n` days. To audit inventory efficiently, the manager needs to answer multiple queries about the total stock added between two days (inclusive).\n\n## Task\nGiven an array `stock` of `n` positive integers where `stock[i]` represents stock added on day `i` (0-indexed), and a list of `q` queries where each query is `[L, R]`, return the total stock added from day `L` to day `R` (inclusive) for each query.\n\n## Function Signature\n```python\ndef range_sum_queries(stock: list[int], queries: list[list[int]]) -> list[int]:\n```\n\n## Input Format\n- First line: integer `n` (size of stock array)\n- Second line: `n` space-separated integers representing `stock`\n- Third line: integer `q` (number of queries)\n- Next `q` lines: two integers `L R` per line\n\n## Output Format\nReturn a list of `q` integers, one per query.",
