    "problem_statement": "## Background\nA bioinformatics tool processes DNA sequences represented as strings containing only the characters `A`, `C`, `G`, and `T`. A segment of the sequence is considered \"pure\" if no nucleotide character repeats within it.\n\n## Task\nGiven a DNA sequence string `dna`, find the length of the longest contiguous segment (substring) in which no character appears more than once. Return this maximum length.\n\n## Function Signature\n```python\ndef longest_pure_segment(dna: str) -> int:\n```\n\n## Input Format\n- A single string `dna` consisting only of characters from `{'A', 'C', 'G', 'T'}`.\n\n## Output Format\nReturn a single integer — the length of the longest segment with all unique characters.",
