    "problem_statement": "## Background\nA logistics company tracks daily profit/loss values for a delivery route over `n` days. Positive values indicate profit and negative values indicate loss. The company wants to find the most profitable contiguous stretch of days, and also report the starting and ending day indices of that stretch.\n\n## Task\nGiven an array `profits` of `n` integers (which may be negative), find the contiguous subarray with the maximum sum. Return a tuple `(max_sum, start, end)` where:\n- `max_sum` is the maximum subarray sum\n- `start` is the 0-indexed start day of the best subarray\n- `end` is the 0-indexed end day of the best subarray (inclusive)\n\nIf multiple subarrays tie for the maximum sum, return the one that starts earliest. If there is still a tie, return the one that ends earliest.\n\n## Function Signature\n```python\ndef max_profit_subarray(profits: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n```\n\n## Input Format\n- A list of `n` integers.\n\n## Output Format\nReturn a tuple of three integers: `(max_sum, start_index, end_index)`.",
