      "optimal": {
        "approach": "Apply Kadane's Algorithm with index tracking. Maintain the current subarray sum and reset it when starting fresh from the current element gives a better value. Track the tentative start of the current window, and only promote it to the confirmed best when a new maximum is found.",
        "code": "def max_profit_subarray(profits):\n    n = len(profits)\n    max_sum = profits[0]       # best sum seen globally\n    current_sum = profits[0]   # sum of the current candidate subarray\n    best_start = 0             # start index of the best subarray found\n    best_end = 0               # end index of the best subarray found\n    temp_start = 0             # tentative start of the current subarray\n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        # If starting fresh at i beats extending: reset current window\n        if profits[i] > current_sum + profits[i]:\n            current_sum = profits[i]\n            temp_start = i     # new candidate subarray begins at i\n        else:\n            current_sum = current_sum + profits[i]\n\n        # Update global best only if strictly better (preserves earliest start)\n        if current_sum > max_sum:\n            max_sum = current_sum\n            best_start = temp_start\n            best_end = i\n\n    return (max_sum, best_start, best_end)",
